How the Auto Backup rewrite works:

No foreground service: react-native-background-actions is replaced by WorkManager background work, so its foreground-service crash can't happen.
Scheduling:
Hourly, plus a run shortly after new photos appear on the device.
Wi-Fi-only, charging-only and battery-not-low conditions are checked by WorkManager at start and re-checked between chunks.
Everything is cancelled when you turn it off.
Persistence: settings and login tokens are kept natively, so they survive restarts, JS reloads and reboots.
Worker flow:
Scan the device's photos and videos.
Skip anything already backed up.
Ask the server which files it already has, and skip those too.
Upload the rest in chunks, saving progress after every chunk so a stopped run resumes.
Mark each item as backed up.
No duplicates: only one backup run can happen at a time.
